{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1535317-running-vampire-s-mortal-lives","id":1535317,"title":"Running Vampire's Mortal-lives.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-08T19:43:49-07:00","id":1535317,"title":"Running Vampire's Mortal-lives.","content":"I'm thinking of running two of my fellow V:tM player's characters, but in a mortals setting; I want to use CoD, as they don't know the ins and outs of that system and won't character-engineer or rule's lawyer (they remember the page number rules are on). <br /> <br /> Here's what I have to base this off of: Gangrel: &quot;My character was embraced in the 15th century in Romania (hello Dracula)(and he likes the Gypsy-book)&quot;. With the Fog of Eternity, well, maybe not so. I'm thinking of playing his character in 16th-century Russia, or later, with his mother being Romanian as an attempt for a local Boyar to be Orthodox-faith. <br /> <br /> Either due to Tartans, Moscovy or the Poles, his family will lose their status and he'll be forced into the role of a gypsy; to wander. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of having a Tartan-rival, join him in his disposed-status, perhaps they have a common enemy? <br /> <br /> Not sure about the embrace; just, I think his sire will, due to his bravery in battle, equate him to, &quot;Lancelot&quot;. In the V:tM, game, he was obsessed with another vampire named, Kathrine (Katerina), could be his mother or potential spouse of his past? <br /> <br /> I have an old vampire-law that every time a new Czar is crowned, the vampires of Moscow and create a new vampire with the name _____of (the Czar), as a way to denote age and status. <br /> <br /> Thinking of giving him a magical-sword (does Agg.), as a reminder of his Viking-roots.<br /> <br /> Elements of his childhood, with will be RPG'd, are an abusive-father, who sent him away to study at a monastery. <br /> <br /> There's several variations going on, given his Grangrel-status such as Wolf-Blooded, maybe? Or perhaps the path of the gypsies. I'm not sure. <br /> <br /> There's also another option: do I make the game with guns or with swords? Given the FoE, I could easily create a game that goes back to the time the Vikings were setting up trade routes to Byzantine or, do I place the game much further in the future, under Peter the Great or Catherine the Great? For a vampire, sooner is more possible than later on in the past. <br /> <br /> That's one things about a Requiem-game, you can play immortality and have the decades fly by, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}